    {
      "id": "f2b000455d2cd5da553801b8b714accf3714cd50",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3092596605,
          "type": null,
          "body": "You guys are too fast for me with merging ;-) Some remark in comparing file paths. I know that currently we just reimplementing the way it was done before. But I think that is wrong. If we already are utilising Qt6, we should also utilise QFileInfo. There are a couple of reasons for that:\n\n- QFileInfo takes care of // vs \\ vs \\/ vs \\\\ shenanigans when copying file paths or reusing stored file paths. So we dont really have to consider Windows or not. \n- It will also take care of network paths vs locally mounted paths (e.g. Mac / Linux) and correctly compare those.\n- macOS HFS+/APFS is case-insensitive by default (but can be configured as\n  case-sensitive)\n- Windows NTFS directories can be marked case-sensitive since Windows 10 1803                                                                  \n- Path normalization — symlinks, ../, ./, trailing slashes, and drive letter casing  \n\nIt works also on non-existing file paths. It basically just verifies that the file path is correctly formatted. Additionally you can could check if it exists. I'll write up a small patch for this change here to utilise it and add you guys as reviewers.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-02-18T09:32:54.421Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-02-18T09:37:30.995Z",
